.TH PHYLLO-CHECK 1 "Phyllotaxis" "phyllo" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
phyllo-check \- validate project integration and report Utility advisories
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B phyllo check
.RB [ --format
.BR text | json ]
.RB [ --quiet ]
.RB [ --no-color ]
.RB [ --scope
.BR venation ]
.br
.B phyllo check --help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B phyllo check
discovers the nearest project root and installed Phyllotaxis package,
reads inert project configuration and canonical contract metadata, and
validates the Venation CSS contract. With no explicit scope and an effective
Utility visual profile, it also inspects local consumer CSS and HTML for
non-failing visual-conformance advisories. Editorial projects skip Utility
visual advisories. It does not change project files, execute project code, or
perform network lookups for advisory analysis.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --format text|json
Select human-readable text or the versioned JSON result. Text is the default.
JSON diagnostics are included in the result's diagnostics array.
.TP
.B --quiet
Suppress successful human-readable output and informational diagnostics.
Warnings and errors remain on standard error. Quiet mode does not change JSON
diagnostics or alter the exit status.
.TP
.B --scope venation
Select the Venation-only validation scope. This is the only supported explicit
scope and does not run Utility visual advisories.
.TP
.B --no-color
Disable ANSI color in human output. This is also implied by non-TTY output, NO_COLOR, or TERM=dumb.
.TP
.B --help
Display command help on standard output without discovering a project.
.SH OUTPUT
In human mode, success is printed to standard output and warning/error
diagnostics to standard error; informational diagnostics are also printed unless
--quiet is set. With --format json, the required envelope includes schemaVersion,
command, ok, and diagnostics regardless of --quiet. Paths, when present, are
project-root-relative; line, when present, is 1-based. Warning and informational
advisories do not make ok false.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Validation completed with no error-level violations. Warning/informational
advisories may be present.
.TP
.B 1
Validation completed with contract violations.
.TP
.B 2
Usage, configuration, or required package resolution error.
.TP
.B 3
Operational error prevented validation.
.TP
.B 4
Unexpected internal CLI failure.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted by SIGINT where the platform/runtime uses conventional signal propagation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR phyllo (1)
.br
docs/cli/phyllo.md in the source repository documents the canonical command contract.
